# The `vstd` functions the workspace's crates may call, by path, each with why it is sound for any caller. Verus'
# library holds functions sound only for verified callers (its pointers, cells, atomics, and locks) and wrappers that
# reach `std` behind the doors (its threads and hash maps), so a call outside this list fails the typed lint.
vstd::pervasive::VecAdditionalExecFns::set	stores a vector's element through std's own checked indexing (`self[i] = value`), so an index out of range panics as it does for any caller
<std::vec::Vec<T> as vstd::pervasive::VecAdditionalExecFns<T>>::set	stores a vector's element through std's own checked indexing (`self[i] = value`), so an index out of range panics as it does for any caller
